<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῐνύσκω</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῐνύσσω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίνυσσα</span>: aor.
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπινύσθην</span> :— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make prudent, admonish,
			correct</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤδη γάρ με καὶ ἄλλο τεὴ ἐπίνυσσεν
					ἐφετμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.249
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφραδέοντα πινυσσέμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Naumach.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.23.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκεῖνον . . πινύσκετ᾽ εὐλόγοισι
					νουθετήμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					830
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερδαλέῳ μύθῳ σε πινύσκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Dian.</u>
					152
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπόταν πινύσκῃ ζεὺς ἄματα</span>
			<i>makes</i> the days <i>calm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				12
			</span></i>; simply, <i>teach</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταλασήϊα ἔργα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					178
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τᾶς ματρὸς
			πινυσθείς</span> Pythag ap. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>VP</u>
				28.146
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπνυμαι</span>.)</div>
